.TH GRADEBOOK\-TESTS 1 "2026-09" "gradebook" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gradebook-tests \- score how effective a repository's test suite actually is
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gradebook-tests
.RI [ path ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scores a test suite on what it actually establishes \(em not on coverage
alone \(em and, from the git history, whether the tests tend to arrive with
the code or after it.
.PP
The default path is the current directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
.BR text ,
.B json
or
.B markdown
(default text).
.TP
.BI \-\-fail\-under " N"
Exit 1 when the score is below N. The CI gate.
.TP
.BI \-\-baseline " FILE"
A previous
.B "\-\-format json"
report to diff against.
.TP
.BR \-\-fail\-on\-drop " [\fIN\fR]"
With
.BR \-\-baseline ,
exit 1 when the score drops by more than N (default 0).
.TP
.B \-\-by\-dir
Also score each immediate subdirectory that holds code.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-git
Skip the git-history TDD analysis.
.TP
.BI \-\-top " N"
How many recommendations to show (default 5).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-flags " N"
Cap the red flags listed (default all; 0 hides them).
.TP
.B \-\-list\-dimensions
Print the scoring model and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Scored, and no gate was breached.
.TP
.B 1
The score was below
.BR \-\-fail\-under ,
or dropped past
.BR \-\-fail\-on\-drop .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Score the suite:
.PP
.RS
.B gradebook-tests
.RE
.PP
Without reading git history:
.PP
.RS
.B gradebook-tests \-\-no\-git \-\-format markdown
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gradebook-code (1).
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/gradebook
.UE
